# Platform strategy 2026 — platform development plan received 26 September 2026
#
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HANDLING NOTE — PLATFORM-PLAN-HANDLING-2026-09-26
#
# This block is the ONLY statement of how this object is handled. The corpus README and the
# Sprint 21 bootstrap README cite the identifier above rather than restating it.
# `tests/lint/test_nso_corpus_manifest_integrity.py` fails loudly if a registered citation goes
# stale or if this definition moves.
#
# 1. WHAT THE OBJECT IS.
#    PLATFORM_DEVELOPMENT_PLAN_2026-09-26.txt is a proposed five-phase, twenty-week plan to
#    rebuild this repository as a multi-technology, multi-jurisdiction web platform. The project
#    owner supplied it in a Claude Code cloud session on 26 September 2026 with the instruction
#    "analyze, evaluate, memorize, add to corpus and discuss", for the next sprint. The supplier
#    did not state its author or origin, and this record does not infer one.
#
# 2. FIDELITY.
#    The file holds the plan text as the session received it, from "To transform" to "project
#    finance platform.". The owner's instruction, which preceded the plan in the same message, is
#    quoted in section 1 rather than stored in the file. One terminal newline was added. Nothing
#    else was changed: wording, errors, list markers, the five en dashes, the six multiplication
#    signs and the inline formula are preserved as received. The chat transport may have
#    normalised whitespace or list markers relative to the author's original, which this
#    repository cannot see. The hash below pins the bytes that were received and evaluated.
#
# 3. PUBLICATION.
#    The full text is published in this public repository, because the owner asked for it to be
#    added to the corpus. Before commit it was read in full for restricted content. It carries no
#    confidentiality marking, no third-party commercial terms or prices, no counterparty names
#    and no personal data. A push to this repository is effectively irreversible. The owner was
#    then offered the manifest-only route used for the NSO commercial offers and the Kalpitiya
#    wind package, and on 26 September 2026, in the same session, decided to keep the full text
#    public, replying "keep on public branch". That reply is the recorded authority for this
#    publication (decision D4 of the Sprint 21 bootstrap).
#
# 4. STATUS: RECORDED, NOT ACCEPTED.
#    The plan is a proposal, not evidence of any fact about this model, its projects, or the law
#    and methods it describes. Its statements about the repository, tax law, reference rates and
#    debt sizing were checked in the evaluation, and several are wrong. Nothing in it is adopted,
#    scheduled or authorized by this record. The evaluation is in docs/SPRINT_21_BOOTSTRAP/.
#
